519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787507493609107001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\n\n`scripts/check_server_manifest.py` currently compares only environment variable names. `server.json` publishes `name`, `description`, and `isRequired` for each record, so description drift, requiredness drift, and duplicate records can pass the current gate. `rebar.mcp_server.MCP_ENV_VARS` remains the canonical inventory. The F05 generated ownership catalog remains deferred and is outside this task.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Refactor the checker to normalize complete `name`, `description`, and `isRequired` records from the canonical inventory and `server.json`.\n- Reject duplicate names in either inventory before comparison.\n- Report missing, extra, and changed records with enough field detail to identify the correction.\n- Add focused checker tests for the clean manifest, each changed field, and duplicate detection.\n- Preserve the existing CI entry point and MCP authentication contract coverage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The committed `server.json` passes comparison against normalized canonical records.\n- [ ] A description mismatch causes a nonzero checker result and identifies the affected name.\n- [ ] An `isRequired` mismatch causes a nonzero checker result and identifies the affected name.\n- [ ] A duplicate name in either inventory causes a nonzero checker result.\n- [ ] Focused checker and MCP manifest contract tests pass.\n- [ ] Lint and type checking pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/check_server_manifest.py","reason":"Compare complete normalized environment records and reject duplicates."},{"path":"server.json","reason":"Keep the published environment records aligned with 